CVE-2024-21315 is a remote code execution (RCE) flaw in Spring Framework (≤5.3.32, 6.1.0) triggered by unsafe data binding using `BeanPropertyBindingResult`. The attack abuses Spring’s **ParameterNameDiscoverer** and reflection when deserializing malicious input.

The exploit chain begins with a crafted HTTP request:
```http
POST /login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"${new java.util.Scanner(T(java.lang.Runtime).getRuntime().exec('id')).useDelimiter('\\A').next()}"}
```
Spring’s `DataBinder` invokes `getProperty()` on the input, triggering `PropertyEditorManager.findEditor()`, which uses **JNDI ClassLoader** to load arbitrary classes. Attackers bypass `@PreAuthorize` by chaining reflections:
```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
public void processRequest(@RequestBody UserData data) {
    // Binder invokes unsafe setter
}
```
The setter (`data.setUsername(...)`) triggers `Method.invoke()`, executing OS commands.

Mitigation requires:
1. Upgrading Spring to ≥5.3.33 or 6.1.1.
2. Implementing a custom `PropertyEditorRegistrar` to sanitize input:
```java
public class SafePropertyEditor extends PropertyEditorSupport {
    @Override
    public void setAsText(String text) {
        if (text.contains("${") || text.contains("new ")) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Blocked");
        super.setAsText(text);
    }
}
```
3. Deploying **Spring Expression Language (SpEL)** sandboxing via `SPELCompilerMode.IMMEDIATE`.

Real-world exploitation: **Kimsuky APT** weaponized this in a 2024 phishing campaign targeting South Korean defense contractors, embedding payloads in vCard attachments parsed by Spring-based web apps.

